This private benchmark extraction implements the tilted-ring method of
E. M. Di Teodoro and F. Fraternali, using BBarolo revision
2a780fe3c933eb81fd767a3bda17964a9eca2936. Original BBarolo core headers
permit GNU GPL version2 or any later version; their copyright and warranty
notice is preserved by the accompanying LICENSE. Some older documentation
mentions GPL3; GPL3 is within the core's GPL2-or-later choice. No MIT or
other license is inferred for the original core.

The isolated original uses CFITSIO, WCSLIB and FFTW. Those packages and the
original binaries are not imported or redistributed as task runtime code.
The cleaned runtime and standalone evaluator use general NumPy and SciPy.

The unchanged NGC2403 FITS observation is an author-distributed example
whose header identifies VLA data and the original acquisition. No separate
explicit data redistribution license was located. The code license is not
asserted to license the observation. This package is staged for the user's
authorized local research; wider publication/redistribution rights remain
unresolved. The paper's availability likewise is not a data license.

The original initialization copy reads beyond a40-element prepass array
when41 rings are requested. All original failed/successful-but-undefined
runs are retained privately. A minimal bounds-only qualification copies
only available prepass elements and preserves the supplied initialization
on the unmatched last ring, with all41 target rings still fitted. Labels
"qualified original" refer to that route. They do not claim unchanged
upstream execution or independent kinematic truth.
